      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-09-23_WidnesExaminer_art0043" n="art0043">
        <head>Picotees.</head>
        <p>Picotees.</p>
        <p>Yellow grounds, Exquisite; Onward, John Ruskin, Her Majesty, Othello, Togo, Dago, M. Lennox, Montezuma, Mrs. J. J. Keen, Santa Claus and F. W. Goodfellow; white grounds, A. Robsart, Favourite, Fair Maiden, Lavinia, Mrs. G. Chaundy, Thomas William, Lady Ethel, Mrs. Sharp, W. E. Dickson,' Radiant, Mrs. Hammond and S. Obaldiston. October is thee best month to plant, and catalogues may be. had' from the carnation specialists.</p>
        <p>Cuttings of all kinds may be taken now; insert in sandy soil and keep near the glass. Chrysanthemums may be disbudded if size of bloom is desired, and plants will be well bene- fited by an application of liquid manure. Strawberry beds may be made from runners from the old plants; plant 15in. apart, not too deep, in well-manured land. Dig up all vacant land for the sun to sweeten it and land intended to grow cabbage for spring cutting should be well,limed; the latter being the best preventative for club root. Burn all garden rubbish or store in hole and cover with soil to rot for use as manure for following season. Kidney beans have been a success this sea- son, Canadian Wonder and Ne Plus Ultra doing very welt Wood's Centenary or Wax Podded is a grand dwarf kidney bean, giving large, -thick, yellow pods, quite stringless and grand flavour, and readers should try this bean next season.</p>
