      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-09-23_WidnesExaminer_art0096" n="art0096">
        <head>" MISS9NG."</head>
        <p>" MISS9NG."</p>
        <p>Suspense in The Case C Lance- Corporal KnoMes.</p>
        <p>The uncertainty and suspense attaching to the fate of Lance-Corporal Robt. Parr Knowles, King's Liverpools, son Of Mr. W. Knowles, 14, Hewitt-street, is still further complicated this week by the receipt of a second official notifica- tion that lie has been "missing" since the engagement on the 30th July. It will be remembered he was first "unoffi- cially" reported killed on that day, which has been partially confirmed since by the return of letters -marked "Killed in action." But the War Office reports do not confirm this, their first report being that he waa" wounded" and the second one as "missing," both conveying a gleam of hope, which possibly may yet be realised.</p>
