        <p>Mrs. E. Lawton, of 36, Marbury-street, Latchford, Warrington, says :—" I believe my kidney trouble was brought on by catch- ing a chill after having a bad back. I suffered terribly with my back after that. I was laid up for three weeks at a time, and the pain was so acute that I dared not turn from one side to the other. I was de- pressed and low-spirited, and seemed to have lost all my energy. The kidney excretions were unnatural and there was distress in relieving the bladder. " Doan's Backache Sidney Pills did me good fPom the first, and after I had given the pills a fair trial I lost all the pain, the kidney weakness was corrected, and I felt like a new woman in health. I can recom- mend Doan's Pills because they did me so much good."</p>
        <p>(Signed) ". E. Lawton." Be sure you ask for DOAN'S and get DOAN'S—the Pills Mrs. Lawton had.</p>
        <p>Webb (4). J. Heywood (4), G. Willcock (4), A" Atherton, (4), J. Broadhurst (F.) (4), J. Spilsburf • (2), I. Barlow (1), W. White (4), J. Pennine")a, (4). A. E. HaAds (3), T. Davies (4). H. Green (3/' S. Taylor (3), T. Litton (5), W. Buckley (5). Barton (2), W. Randles (scr.). John Appleton (scr.)•</p>
