        <head>HOUSE ON FIRE LAST NIGIIT.</head>
        <p>HOUSE ON FIRE LAST NIGIIT.</p>
        <p>During the temporary absence at the Pall and Hippodrome of Mr. and Mrs. Crane, West-street, a fire broke out at their residerl about nine o'clock last ,night. The Fire gade was summoned, and, in the meanthe , buckets of water were effectively used ,by t, neighbours. The outbreqk was subdued in aboub twenty minutes, but no before the kitchen had been badly damaged • Printed and published by John Walker andll C°- (Warrington) Limited, at the Ex1)1°11. General Printing Works, Bewsey-street, 1V11: rington; also published by them nti EXAMINER Offices, 2, Victoria-road, Wiallest' 32, George-street, St. Edens; 3, Market-stree .Earlestown, all in the County of Lancastert' and at Church-street, Runcorn, in. the Coun of Chester,</p>
